# Rank 1733 / CVE-2021-37580 (CWE-287): ShenYu Admin's dashboard login
# decided authentication from a JWT payload nobody had signed-check.
# ShiroRealm.doGetAuthenticationInfo is Shiro's authentication callback --
# returning a non-null AuthenticationInfo there means the token is
# authentic -- and it read the identity straight out of the token through
# JwtUtils.getIssuer, which is com.auth0.jwt's
# JWT.decode(token).getClaim("userName").asString(). JWT.decode is the
# java-jwt API documented as decoding "without verifying the signature",
# so the userName claim of any base64 blob named the principal, and
# getUserInfoByToken returned SimpleAuthenticationInfo for it. The signing
# half had the same defect from the other side: generateAlgorithm() took
# the HMAC key from a @ConfigurationProperties bean whose shipped default
# in application.yml is `key: 2095132720951327`, so the published literal
# is also the verification key. The fixed revision (f78adb2) inlines the lookup into
# doGetAuthenticationInfo, adds `if (!JwtUtils.verifyToken(token,
# dashboardUserVO.getPassword())) throw new AuthenticationException(...)`
# before the SimpleAuthenticationInfo, deletes generateAlgorithm/
# verifierToken/getIssuerDate, re-keys generateToken on the user's own
# password, and turns the config key into `expired-seconds`. Remediation
# confirmed present at f78adb2.
#
# ATTENTION, both halves of the discrimination are the project's own
# vocabulary. The wiring-not-dataflow family of ranks 1514/1535/1540/1556/
# 1557/1593, with the 1380 counterweight failing the same way it did at
# 1624 (PyJWT's crit header) and 1621 (PwnDoc's stale role claim): the
# remediation's only trace inside the guarded method is the call to
# JwtUtils.verifyToken, a project-local static, not a library API -- the
# library's own verification call (JWT.require(...).build().verify(...))
# stays inside verifyToken, one function away from the sink. A negation
# keyed on that name fails the rename test (1394). And the function that
# actually carries the unverified decode, JwtUtils.getIssuer, is
# byte-identical at both revisions, so a binding on JWT.decode fires on
# the change rather than discriminating it. Measured with a throwaway
# presence binding (function contains JWT.decode and not JWT.require,
# emitting code.JwtUnverified) against the checkout at f78adb2^ and at
# f78adb2: one VYQL-CFG-005 row each, JwtUtils.java:63 at the parent and
# JwtUtils.java:61 at the fixed revision -- the same unchanged getIssuer -- so it is
# a false positive on the remediated revision, not coverage. Confirmed at
# spec level too: with that probe binding in place the runner reports
# VYQL-CFG-005 on the patched-form snippet below while satisfying the
# expect on the unverified one, so this spec is a double miss by
# construction rather than by accident. That binding
# is also unmeasurable rather than merely clean: com.auth0.jwt appears in
# exactly one file across the ~356 rank clones and in zero files of the
# Java benchmark corpus. Nothing else is available either -- vyql match on
# JwtUtils.java labels only the log calls and on ShiroRealm.java labels
# nothing at all, while vyql resolve resolves the whole intra-project
# chain (getUserInfoByToken -> JwtUtils.getIssuer -> JWT.decode ->
# SimpleAuthenticationInfo; a VYQL-INJ-009 path in the real scan walks
# generateToken -> getIssuer -> verifyToken end to end), so resolution is
# not the blocker and neither is the lambda: getClaim, though it emits no
# Call node of its own, does reach the function's callPath tokens and the
# probe above fired with it required. Keying the HMAC key on its
# configuration origin is worse than useless: reading a signing secret
# from a @ConfigurationProperties bean is the correct Spring pattern, so
# that shape would flag every properly-configured deployment. Concepts
# considered and rejected: code.JwtUnverified / code.UnverifiedJwt (fire
# on getIssuer at both revisions -- measured above), code.WeakJwtSecret
# (the secret is a YAML default, not a Java literal, and
# hardcodedSecretLiteral460's evidence is secret-named string literals
# only). No ENGINE-GAPS.md entry: no taint path is interrupted and no
# construct is mishandled; what does not exist is vocabulary for "this
# project-local call verifies a JWT signature", which is a fact about the
# caller, not the library. No definition change shipped. Spec
# cve_rank1733 records the unverified authentication path and the
# verifying form, both asserting reject VYQL-AUTH-108 and VYQL-CFG-005:
# when caller-aware unverified-decode vocabulary lands, the unverified
# form must flip to expect while the verifying form stays reject.

test "rank1733: the realm returns a principal built from an unverified decode"
  lang java
  file shenyu-admin/src/main/java/org/apache/shenyu/admin/shiro/config/ShiroRealm.java
  reject VYQL-AUTH-108
  reject VYQL-CFG-005
  code
  ```
  package org.apache.shenyu.admin.shiro.config;

  import org.apache.commons.lang3.StringUtils;
  import org.apache.shenyu.admin.model.custom.UserInfo;
  import org.apache.shenyu.admin.model.vo.DashboardUserVO;
  import org.apache.shenyu.admin.service.DashboardUserService;
  import org.apache.shenyu.admin.utils.JwtUtils;
  import org.apache.shiro.authc.AuthenticationException;
  import org.apache.shiro.authc.AuthenticationInfo;
  import org.apache.shiro.authc.AuthenticationToken;
  import org.apache.shiro.authc.SimpleAuthenticationInfo;
  import org.apache.shiro.realm.AuthorizingRealm;

  public class ShiroRealm extends AuthorizingRealm {

      private final DashboardUserService dashboardUserService;

      @Override
      public boolean supports(final AuthenticationToken token) {
          return token instanceof StatelessToken;
      }

      @Override
      protected AuthenticationInfo doGetAuthenticationInfo(final AuthenticationToken authenticationToken) {
          String token = (String) authenticationToken.getCredentials();
          if (StringUtils.isEmpty(token)) {
              return null;
          }

          UserInfo userInfo = getUserInfoByToken(token);

          return new SimpleAuthenticationInfo(userInfo, token, this.getName());
      }

      private UserInfo getUserInfoByToken(final String token) {

          String userName = JwtUtils.getIssuer(token);
          if (StringUtils.isEmpty(userName)) {
              throw new AuthenticationException("userName is null");
          }

          DashboardUserVO dashboardUserVO = dashboardUserService.findByUserName(userName);
          if (dashboardUserVO == null) {
              throw new AuthenticationException(String.format("userName(%s) can not be found.", userName));
          }

          return UserInfo.builder()
                  .userName(userName)
                  .userId(dashboardUserVO.getId())
                  .build();
      }
  }
  ```
  file shenyu-admin/src/main/java/org/apache/shenyu/admin/utils/JwtUtils.java
  ```
  package org.apache.shenyu.admin.utils;

  import com.auth0.jwt.JWT;
  import com.auth0.jwt.JWTVerifier;
  import com.auth0.jwt.algorithms.Algorithm;
  import com.auth0.jwt.interfaces.DecodedJWT;
  import java.util.Date;
  import java.util.Optional;

  public final class JwtUtils {

      public static String getIssuer(final String token) {
          DecodedJWT jwt = JWT.decode(token);
          return Optional.ofNullable(jwt).map(item -> item.getClaim("userName").asString()).orElse("");
      }

      public static String generateToken(final String userName) {
          return JWT.create().withClaim("userName", userName).withExpiresAt(new Date()).sign(generateAlgorithm());
      }

      private static DecodedJWT verifierToken(final String token) {
          JWTVerifier verifier = JWT.require(generateAlgorithm()).build();
          return verifier.verify(token);
      }

      private static Algorithm generateAlgorithm() {
          JwtProperties properties = SpringBeanUtils.getInstance().getBean(JwtProperties.class);
          return Algorithm.HMAC256(properties.getKey());
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1733: the realm verifies the token before returning the principal"
  lang java
  file shenyu-admin/src/main/java/org/apache/shenyu/admin/shiro/config/ShiroRealm.java
  reject VYQL-AUTH-108
  reject VYQL-CFG-005
  code
  ```
  package org.apache.shenyu.admin.shiro.config;

  import org.apache.commons.lang3.StringUtils;
  import org.apache.shenyu.admin.model.custom.UserInfo;
  import org.apache.shenyu.admin.model.vo.DashboardUserVO;
  import org.apache.shenyu.admin.service.DashboardUserService;
  import org.apache.shenyu.admin.utils.JwtUtils;
  import org.apache.shiro.authc.AuthenticationException;
  import org.apache.shiro.authc.AuthenticationInfo;
  import org.apache.shiro.authc.AuthenticationToken;
  import org.apache.shiro.authc.SimpleAuthenticationInfo;
  import org.apache.shiro.realm.AuthorizingRealm;

  public class ShiroRealm extends AuthorizingRealm {

      private final DashboardUserService dashboardUserService;

      @Override
      public boolean supports(final AuthenticationToken token) {
          return token instanceof StatelessToken;
      }

      @Override
      protected AuthenticationInfo doGetAuthenticationInfo(final AuthenticationToken authenticationToken) {
          String token = (String) authenticationToken.getCredentials();
          if (StringUtils.isEmpty(token)) {
              return null;
          }

          String userName = JwtUtils.getIssuer(token);
          if (StringUtils.isEmpty(userName)) {
              throw new AuthenticationException("userName is null");
          }

          DashboardUserVO dashboardUserVO = dashboardUserService.findByUserName(userName);
          if (dashboardUserVO == null) {
              throw new AuthenticationException(String.format("userName(%s) can not be found.", userName));
          }

          if (!JwtUtils.verifyToken(token, dashboardUserVO.getPassword())) {
              throw new AuthenticationException("token is error.");
          }

          return new SimpleAuthenticationInfo(UserInfo.builder()
                  .userName(userName)
                  .userId(dashboardUserVO.getId())
                  .build(), token, this.getName());
      }
  }
  ```
  file shenyu-admin/src/main/java/org/apache/shenyu/admin/utils/JwtUtils.java
  ```
  package org.apache.shenyu.admin.utils;

  import com.auth0.jwt.JWT;
  import com.auth0.jwt.JWTVerifier;
  import com.auth0.jwt.algorithms.Algorithm;
  import com.auth0.jwt.interfaces.DecodedJWT;
  import java.util.Date;
  import java.util.Optional;

  public final class JwtUtils {

      private static final long TOKEN_EXPIRE_SECONDS = 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000L;

      public static String getIssuer(final String token) {
          DecodedJWT jwt = JWT.decode(token);
          return Optional.ofNullable(jwt).map(item -> item.getClaim("userName").asString()).orElse("");
      }

      public static String generateToken(final String userName, final String key) {
          return generateToken(userName, key, null);
      }

      public static String generateToken(final String userName, final String key, final Long expireSeconds) {
          return JWT.create()
                  .withClaim("userName", userName)
                  .withExpiresAt(new Date(System.currentTimeMillis() + Optional.ofNullable(expireSeconds).orElse(TOKEN_EXPIRE_SECONDS)))
                  .sign(Algorithm.HMAC256(key));
      }

      public static boolean verifyToken(final String token, final String key) {
          JWTVerifier verifier = JWT.require(Algorithm.HMAC256(key)).build();
          verifier.verify(token);
          return true;
      }
  }
  ```
